.TH "INSPEKT\-EVAL" "1" "2026\-04\-16" "Inspekt 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inspekt\-eval \- Execute arbitrary JavaScript code in the browser
context.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]inspekt\f[R] \f[B]eval\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] [\f[I]CODE\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Execute arbitrary JavaScript code in the browser context.
.PP
Runs JavaScript in the page\(cqs execution context with full DOM access.
The code can:
.IP \(bu 2
Access and modify the DOM
.IP \(bu 2
Call page\(cqs JavaScript functions
.IP \(bu 2
Use browser APIs (localStorage, fetch, etc.)
.IP \(bu 2
Return values (primitives, objects, arrays)
.PP
The result is serialized and returned.
Async code is supported \- return a Promise and it will be awaited.
.PP
Security note: This is a powerful capability.
The executed code runs with the page\(cqs privileges, not the
extension\(cqs.
.PP
Timeout defaults to 30 seconds for long\-running operations.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\f[I]CODE\f[R]
optional text argument
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-f\f[R], \f[B]\(enfile\f[R], \f[I]PATH\f[R]
Execute code from file
.TP
\f[B]\-t\f[R], \f[B]\(entimeout\f[R], \f[I]FLOAT\f[R]
Timeout in seconds (default: 10)
.TP
\f[B]\(enformat\f[R], \f[I][auto|json|raw]\f[R]
Output format (default: \f[CR]auto\f[R])
.TP
\f[B]\(enurl\f[R]
Also print page URL
.TP
\f[B]\(entitle\f[R]
Also print page title
.TP
\f[B]\(enno\-console\f[R]
Don\(cqt show console output
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
inspekt eval \(aqdocument.title\(aq
inspekt eval \(aqdocument.querySelectorAll(\(dqa\(dq).length\(aq
inspekt eval \(aqawait fetch(\(dq/api/data\(dq).then(r => r.json())\(aq
inspekt eval \(dqdocument.title\(dq
.EE
